error[E0508]: cannot pass `p` as `mut` twice in one call
   --> tests/programs/functions/mut_params/e0508.la:10:14
   |
10 |     both(mut p, mut p);
   |              ^      - `p` is passed as `mut` here too
   |
   = help: one place can't be changed through two parameters at once: pass two different places

error[E0508]: cannot pass `p` as `mut` and also as another argument
   --> tests/programs/functions/mut_params/e0508.la:11:14
   |
11 |     read(mut p, p);
   |              ^  - `p` is passed here too
   |
   = help: copy it first, so the call reads a value that doesn't change: `let w = p;` and pass `w`

error[E0508]: cannot pass `p.x` as `mut` to a `mut self` method called on `p`
   --> tests/programs/functions/mut_params/e0508.la:12:15
   |
12 |     p.eat(mut p.x);
   |     -         ^^^
   |     |
   |     `p` is edited by this call
   |
   = help: copy it into a variable, pass that, and put it back: `let mut x = p.x; p.eat(mut x); p.x = x;`

For more about E0508, run `lughac explain E0508`.
